------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A. Proof-of-work components (Apache License, Version 2.0 -- full text in C)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Portions of the binary-field / NOID implementation are derived from hekate-math,
as adapted for Parano1d/NOID by the Parano1d project (Paranoid Zero):
https://github.com/oumuamua-labs/hekate-math

hekate-math
Copyright 2026 Andrei Kochergin and Oumuamua Labs.
NOID adaptation Copyright 2026 Paranoid Zero.

Portions of the field, multilinear-extension, sumcheck, and tensor-algebra
implementation are adapted from binius64:
https://github.com/binius-zk/binius64

Copyright (c) 2025 The Binius Developers
Copyright (c) 2025 Irreducible, Inc.

Portions of the Ligerito polynomial-commitment implementation are ported from
bolt-rs:
https://github.com/bcc-research/bolt-rs

Copyright (c) 2026 Bain Capital Crypto, LP and Ron Rothblum
Modifications copyright 2026 Succinct Labs, Benedikt Bunz, William Wang

Portions of the Jetsam (JTM) proof-of-work implementation -- the TowerHash
sponge and the TowerWalk memory walk, their round constants and test vectors --
are derived from Jetsam:
https://github.com/jetsam-chain/jetsam

Jetsam
Copyright 2026 the Jetsam developers.
Jetsam is itself a derivative work of Parano1d (Copyright 2026 Paranoid Zero).

The Poseidon2b permutation used by both proofs of work is described in
"Poseidon(2)b: Binary Field Versions of Poseidon/Poseidon2", Lorenzo Grassi
et al., IACR ePrint 2025/1893 (https://eprint.iacr.org/2025/1893).

